Strictness restored: "no timed retries" now fakes setTimeout AND requestAnimationFrame and asserts zero scrollTop writes for 1 s after open (verified to fail when a setTimeout→rAF→scrollTop retry is re-inserted); the probe asserts the first commit is hidden.
Fixed: pill counts every arrived row (batches), not a deleted newest row or my own temp→server swap; GroupChat pin released by keyboard and by scrolling away (scrollbar), not only touch/wheel; unread position re-decided on every visit (A→B→A); placeholder rows of the previous DM never position the new one; pill status is an always-mounted live region and focus moves to the list after the jump.
Deviations recorded for Gate 2: (1) the unread divider uses per-message read_at, so it appears in DMs only — group chats have no per-message read state in the client (plan said last_read_at); (2) desktop/mobile/RTL screenshots are not produced in this sandbox (no browser able to reach staging) — the owner's visual check on staging replaces them.

## Follow-up review fixes (/projects/sandbox/reviews/pr1482.md)
$ npx vitest run src/components/messages/ConversationView.scroll-anchoring.vtid-05319.test.tsx   # 10 passed
Fixed: the placeholder guard applies only while the conversation is still fetching (legacy direct threads whose rows carry another thread_id were hidden forever — test added); every switch resets the opening position, and the unread anchor belongs to one visit (A with unread → empty or deep-linked B → A never reuses the first visit's divider — test added); a deep-link open clears the anchor.
Further deviations for Gate 2: (3) GroupChat is not hidden until positioned — its opening position is written in the layout pass before paint (test), late layout is absorbed by the pin; (4) with a deep-link target pinned in GroupChat, only touch / wheel / scroll keys release the pin (a scrollbar drag does not, until the target pin ends); (5) no tests/e2e/staging spec: staging checks for this lane are the Vitest suites in staging-tests.json plus the owner's visual check; a read-only staging spec was not written in this session.
